cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: dataset
title: "CIFAR Synthetic Evidence Corpus"
abstract: "A benchmark for detecting AI-manipulated documentary evidence, comprising 2,490 documentary artifacts spanning three documentary-evidence families (receipts, emails, and business and administrative documents), four manipulation sophistication tiers, and four generator families. The corpus is structured around three commitments that prior document-forgery datasets do not jointly satisfy: source-disjoint training and test pools, ablation-ready shortcut controls recorded in the manifest, and redundant provenance markers on every artifact."
